      <p>Check your project at the end of every lesson. The check tells you whether the project is ready to publish: whether its source is sound, whether every deliverable builds, and whether the built output holds together.</p>
      <ul>
      <li>In the editor, choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong>. The result appears in the <strong>Project Validation</strong> panel.</li>
      <li>From the command line, run <code>dogsbay-xml check .</code> from the project root.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Both run the same check. You do not need to install DITA-OT: the editor and the command line include DITA-OT 4.3.5 and build with it.</p>
      <h2 id="what-it-checks" class="group scroll-mt-20">What it checks<a href="#what-it-checks" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>The check runs three stages in order, and each runs only when the one before it passed:</p>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Stage</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Checks</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
