      <TableRow>
      <TableCell>Build</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Every deliverable in <strong>Manage Deliverables</strong> builds with DITA-OT</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell>Output</TableCell>
      <TableCell>Every link, image, and fragment in the built output leads somewhere</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
      <p>It stops at the first stage that fails, because later stages would only report consequences of the same fault. A broken reference in the source, for example, produces a broken link in the output.</p>
      <p>Health uses the root map and house rules set in the project settings once later stages add them.</p>
