      <p>When a build fails, the check names the deliverable and reports the DITA-OT errors, with their message codes, such as <code>DOTJ046E</code>, when DITA-OT gives one. When the output check fails, it lists each link that leads nowhere, with the page and line that contains it, and the verdict counts them, for example <code>Not ready: 1 link in the built output leads nowhere.</code></p>
      <p>Fix the problem and check again. After a lesson's deliberate-error exercise, undo the change and check again before you continue.</p>
